id: pm-s74dca
title: Refuse unsupported schema dry-run flags before mutation
description: "schema add-type accepts the globally declared --dry-run flag but silently drops it and writes types.json, workspace history and merge attributes. Refuse unsupported schema preview combinations before dispatch; preserve supported migration and workflow-policy previews."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-25T15:57:47.833Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-25T16:28:16.678Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-25T16:28:15.863Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-25T16:28:15.863Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Unsupported add/remove/preset and shorthand dry-run calls exit with an actionable refusal without changing schema, history or Git merge attributes; supported migration and policy previews remain available; regression fails before the fix and quality gates pass."
parent: pm-e1va
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
repro_steps: In an initialized temporary workspace run pm schema add-type Preview --dry-run; inspect schema/types.json and workspace history. The original CLI exits 0 and persists the type. Generic SDK runAction schema remove-type with dryRun=true likewise deletes an existing type.
resolution: "Added shared SDK preview admission, retained supported migration/policy contracts, and covered CLI shorthand plus top-level/nested runtime options with real disposable-workspace regressions."
expected_result: "Unsupported previews cannot change schema, history or merge attributes; supported previews remain read-only."
actual_result: Red regressions reproduced CLI creation and SDK deletion. Linked 185-test verification and 17 layout/integration checks pass after the guard relocation; manual built-CLI/public-SDK acceptance preserves byte snapshots. Full-source coverage is exactly 100/100/100/100; its sole directory-cap failure is fixed and reverified.
affected_version: 2026.9.25
component: schema
